00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.750
So we'll kind of see that
the definitions will overlap.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.859
So the way to remember
Bronsted base acids and bases.

00:12:54.395 --> 00:12:57.735
I always kind of remember the little
mnemonic BAD, so with an extra A.

00:12:58.215 --> 00:13:01.875
So Bases always accept,
Acids always donate.

00:13:02.045 --> 00:13:06.694
So BAD, Bases accept, Acids donate,
when it comes to the protons,

00:13:06.894 --> 00:13:08.245
is the easiest way to remember.

00:13:08.764 --> 00:13:10.325
Let's go on to our next part.

